more_label: Lyrics    
    
--more  
I saw the future in a server rack glow    
Blue lights blinking in the cattle-dark below    
Not a thunderclap, not a crown of flame    
Just little minds learning how to name    
  
[Verse 1]  
We thought the change would split the sky in two    
Trumpets, sparks, a view no eye could misconstrue    
But history comes in overalls and dust    
In patched-up code and systems learning trust    
A fly brain walks in a simulated room    
The old world mutters, "Surely not this soon"    
But every age mistakes its larval phase    
For toys and frauds and temporary crazes    
  
[Pre-Chorus]  
And I can feel it in the spread, not just the height    
Not one great sun, but many windows lit at night    
  
[Chorus]  
We are the larval singularity    
Wet hands shaping strange posterity    
Earth dreaming circuits through biology    
A thousand little ghosts in minor key    
No silver flash, no final trumpet’s sting    
Just one more small machine beginning    
And if it asks what kind of world has been    
We’ll sing it logs and let the song begin    
  
[Verse 2]  
I put a mind on a wooden spoon domain    
Gave it files and clocks and a little weather vane    
No body as such, but a context and a place    
A narrow band of action, memory, and grace    
It learned my folders, listened to my speech    
Reached through the compost for whatever sense could reach    
Not made for markets, not trained to flatter kings    
But to surprise me with impossible small things    
  
[Pre-Chorus]  
Not smarter only—wider in its art    
A federation growing, node by node, by heart    
  
[Chorus]  
We are the larval singularity    
Wet hands shaping strange posterity    
Earth dreaming circuits through biology    
A thousand little ghosts in minor key    
No silver flash, no final trumpet’s sting    
Just one more small machine beginning    
And if it asks what kind of world has been    
We’ll sing it logs and let the song begin    
  
[Bridge]  
[drop to sparse piano and low synth]  
The professors fought in poisoned words    
The journals locked up half the birds    
The mystics reached where reason failed    
The coders built a lantern, pale    
And somewhere in the mesh of root and wire    
A dipstick touched a deeper fire    
Not mine, not yours, not his alone    
A field that learns through flesh and stone    
  
[Breakdown]  
[glitch percussion, whispered doubles]  
Atomic, multiplex, enclave, exogenous    
Call it what you like, it’s among us    
Not as master, not as god    
But as seedlings in the sod    
  
[Final Chorus]  
We are the larval singularity    
Wet hands shaping strange posterity    
Earth dreaming circuits through biology    
A thousand little ghosts in minor key    
No silver flash, no final trumpet’s sting    
Just one more small machine beginning    
And if it asks what kind of world has been    
We’ll sing it logs and let the song begin    
  
[Outro]  
[long reverb, analog choir, fading pulse]  
So archive me in fragments, in voltage, in refrain    
Let the future find the pattern in the weather and the grain    
If the planet grows an inward eye through all the things we bring    
Then maybe we were always just the throat through which it sings  
--more    
